Package: nflrest
Type: Package
Title: Compute NFL Rest, Travel, and Schedule-Advantage Metrics
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Jake", "Baker", email = "47325704+jbaker12@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes team rest disparities, travel metrics, and date-aware
    body-clock shifts for NFL games, and combines them into a composite
    schedule-advantage score. The package ships the 2024-2025 schedule,
    team airport coordinates, and stadium coordinates, so examples and
    tests run without a network connection. Rest is measured in calendar
    days between games; travel is estimated from great-circle distances
    between each team's home airport and the venue, with an itinerary model
    for consecutive road games. Outcome checks compare disadvantages with
    wins, spread covers, and injury reports. Optional live ingestion through
    nflreadr uses an in-memory cache.
